9131.synopsis:
Waits for a key on the hall of fame page (MTH_KeyJump, its table follows the call): HELP
goes to the first application's help (cr_hlp), RIGHT to MTH_Copyright, ENTER to cr_waitkey;
MENU, UP, DOWN and LEFT wait again.

4481.synopsis:
Diary's MTH commands: the command block that DiaryDOR points to, read by the kernel's MTH
code (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:
Blocks (10 commands), Cursor (23), Edit (14, 2 hidden) and Files (2). Layout: CMD_MARK (0);
one mthcmd record per command (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name,
help page offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again);
TPC_SEP (1) between topics; CMD_MARK.
